From fe082ffe64cc5bfc72f89527c9be4e69a914c2f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 14:13:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 205/211] aimesh: restore factory x_Setting/w_Setting=0 so a
 Reaper box is discoverable as a node; retire QIS at the httpd layer instead

The v1.2.7 QIS removal flipped factory-default x_Setting/w_Setting 0->1
(shared/defaults.c). Side effect (field-confirmed class, root-caused
2026-07-22): a factory-fresh Reaper box can NEVER be onboarded as an
AiMesh node -
 - no_need_obd() (closed rc/prebuild/*/broadcom.o) returns -1 once
   x_Setting==1, so start_obd()/start_eth_obd() never launch obd; the
   box never broadcasts the onboarding probe-request VSIE
   (obd_add_probe_req_vsie) and no CAP search can find it, wireless or
   ethernet. The amas_bdlkey bundled-kit path (services.c) was dead too.
 - w_Setting==1 left lan_wps_oob=disabled (init-broadcom.c), so even a
   discovered box would refuse the WPS onboarding enrollment.

Fix: restore the STOCK factory defaults (0/0) and keep the first-boot
QIS wizard retired at the web layer instead of via the nvram flag:

 - shared/defaults.c: x_Setting/w_Setting factory defaults back to 0/0
   (non-DEMOUI branch; the ASUS_EULA/ASUS_NEW_EULA pre-signs stay).
 - httpd/httpd.c is_firsttime(): hard-forced 0 - '/' always routes to
   the login page, never QIS_default.cgi. web_hook.o (closed) links
   against this source definition, so blob callers see the same answer.
 - httpd/httpd.c: the three x_Setting==0 pre-auth allowances are
   permanently disabled so a factory box keeps demanding login exactly
   like every v1.2.7..v1.7.1 build (where x_Setting was always 1):
   MIME_EXCEPTION_NOAUTH_FIRST auth skip, the repeater
   start_apply2/apscan login-IP accounting skip, and the pre-auth QIS
   token mint (QIS_default.cgi/page_default.cgi/posted x_Setting=1 ->
   send_token_headers).
 - www/state.js first-run gate 2: w_Setting==0 boxes now route to the
   same first-run wireless page as gate 3
   (Advanced_Wireless_Content.asp?firstboot=1, already in
   reaper_inject.c reaper_skip[] - standing rule 27) instead of the
   retired QIS wireless mini-wizard; self-exempts the target page and
   QIS_* (the AiMesh add-node wizard runs framed).
 - httpd/reaper_inject.c + www/index.asp: comments updated to the new
   design (QIS_wizard.htm stays skip-listed for the framed AiMesh
   add-node flow).

Configured/upgraded boxes are unaffected: persisted nvram keeps
x_Setting/w_Setting=1, and the stock web.c auto-flip restores 1/1 on
the first real apply of a factory box configured as a router (which
also stops obd). A box intended as a NODE just gets factory-reset with
this firmware and left for the CAP's search to find - stock semantics.

Shared source, all 5 models inherit at their next branch bump. NOT
built yet - rides the next build rung with the rest of the batch.
Metal owed: factory box discoverable + full onboard (wireless + eth),
router-path first boot unchanged (login at '/', no QIS, no pre-auth
token), obd gone after configuration ('rc no_need_obd' debug hook).

This does NOT address the separate CAP-side field report (BE98-pair
routers not finding STOCK nodes) - that triage is tracked separately.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
